If a clinician continues an opioid-therapy for a subacute-pain and the clinician prescribes an opioid at a dosage then the clinician should prescribe the opioid cautiously at the dosage.
If a clinician continues an opioid-therapy for a chronic-pain and the clinician prescribes an opioid at a dosage then the clinician should prescribe the opioid cautiously at the dosage.
If a clinician continues an opioid-therapy for a subacute-pain and a dosage-increase-avoidance is possible then the clinician should generally avoid a dosage-increase.
If a clinician continues an opioid-therapy for a chronic-pain and a dosage-increase-avoidance is possible then the clinician should generally avoid a dosage-increase.
